WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.700
Picture a drop of pond water under a microscope.

2
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.740
A Paramecium swims across it.

3
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.960
It is one cell, shaped a bit like a slipper.

4
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:19.020
That one cell moves, eats, and gets rid of extra water and wastes.

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.540
It can also divide in two.

6
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.660
Your body does the same kinds of jobs.

7
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.000
So why does your body have trillions of cells?

8
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:33.830
A living thing made of just one cell is called unicellular.

9
00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:36.530
A Paramecium is unicellular.

10
00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:41.790
Short, hair-like parts called cilia beat to push it along.

11
00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:46.110
Food goes into small sacs called food vacuoles.

12
00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:51.230
A sac called a contractile vacuole squeezes out extra water.

13
00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:55.190
One cell has parts for every life job.

14
00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.740
A living thing made of many cells is called multicellular.

15
00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.280
You are multicellular, and so is an oak tree.

16
00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:08.180
In a many-celled body, cells share the work.

17
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.420
This sharing is called division of labor.

18
00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.840
A specialized cell has a shape and parts that suit one kind of job.

19
00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:19.023
Look at some shapes.

20
00:01:19.943 --> 00:01:22.243
A muscle cell is long and thin.

21
00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:24.623
It shortens to pull on bones.

22
00:01:25.783 --> 00:01:27.803
A nerve cell has long branches.

23
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:30.643
It carries signals over long distances.

24
00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:35.003
A red blood cell is a small, flexible disc.

25
00:01:35.663 --> 00:01:39.143
It carries oxygen and bends through very narrow vessels.

26
00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.407
Cells are grouped into levels.

27
00:01:43.487 --> 00:01:47.507
Similar cells doing one job form a tissue, such as muscle tissue.

28
00:01:48.547 --> 00:01:52.467
Different tissues working together form an organ, such as the heart.

29
00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:58.367
Organs working together form an organ system, such as the heart and blood vessels.

30
00:01:59.287 --> 00:02:01.887
All the systems together make the organism.

31
00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:05.660
The levels depend on each other.

32
00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:09.500
If heart tissue is damaged, the whole body can suffer.

33
00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:14.480
So how can one cell do everything a whole body does?

34
00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.880
A Paramecium does it with the parts of one cell.

35
00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:25.980
A body shares the jobs among trillions of cells, grouped into tissues, organs and organ systems.
